Fillets: a rounding riding on another's contact line ends, at a vertex of
its own edge, where the line ends on the arc of the face that runs from
that vertex (mitcad#1499).

A roof slab's end face F along a slope, its two edges rounded with 1, the
underside's rounding B riding on the slope's contact line on F (1640). At
the eave B's contact on the underside leaves it at the section through the
eave's inner vertex V, the line running on to F's edge with the eave (the
arc from V to the eave's tip). B's walk stopped at that section with its
point on the line inside F, and the corner at V cut an extension of B's
surface with the eave off the line (PerformIntersectionAtEnd), across the
cut of the slope's rounding at the tip ("OneCorner : fillets have too big
radiuses").

- RideOnOverlap: B's end on the line at its spine's end vertex V, where
  the end of A's line nearest to it lies on an arc of F from V (not a
  vertex), is A's point on that arc; the corner at V cuts B with the face
  at the end between two points on arcs.
- ApplyRides: such a ride along a part of A's line from its end (the other
  end of B inside F, where the line runs on: the slab's ceiling corner) is
  a part ride (1340): partOfContact takes one end of the part that is an
  end of A's contact on the same arc (theSharedEnd), and A's SurfData is
  split once, at B's other end.

